  "content": "Owen Carter is scoring 76.0 over his last ten rounds (June 9 to September 26), and his approach play accounts for most of the loss. His most recent recorded round is September 26, so nothing newer is in the data.\n\n- **Total strokes gained:** -6.74 per round, over 8 rounds that have strokes gained. That puts him 5th of 7 on the team, whose average is -5.79. There is no college figure for this metric. The Tour baseline is 0.\n- **Approach:** -4.16 per round, 6th of 7 on the team. The team average is -3.09. This is the largest loss in his game.\n- **Off the tee:** -0.32 per round, 6th of 7. The team average is +0.41.\n- **Putting:** -2.06 per round, 2nd of 7. The team average is -3.03, so this is relatively strong for this group.\n- **Around the green:** -0.20 per round, 4th of 7. The team average is -0.09.\n- **Greens in regulation:** 61.1% over 144 holes. That is just above the Division I average of 60%. It is below his team's average of 62.8%, which puts him 5th of 7. The Tour figure is 66%.\n\nHis last five rounds were uneven:\n- On September 25 and 26, he shot 74 and 71 in a qualifier.\n- On July 8 to 10, he shot 82, 73 and 74 at Poplar Grove. The 82 had a total strokes gained of -10.96, and the other two were -1.56 and -2.82.\n\nThat 82 pulls his ten-round average up noticeably. Two of the qualifier rounds have no putts or strokes gained recorded, so the strokes gained figures rest on 8 of the 10 rounds.\n\nApproach is the area to work on. His putting is holding up relative to the team.",
